2026-11-05T09:28:27 0x00494410 data ai_Unk494410 -> ai_DecideAcquittal by:main why:the trial's ask-AI callback ai_Unk4de340 answers request kind 4 with it (the voter m[7] .. m[9] = ids[2] .. ids[4], judge and assessors, checked as cm_TrialAskPlayer's case 4): cm_RunTrial sums the three answers into votes and a count under 2 convicts (the PROZESS_7_SCHULDIG path), so 1 is the vote for the accused. The body weighs the accused's (c18) liking of and mix with the voter (gm_Liking, gm_Mix) against the accuser's (c14), the plan's score^2 * 0.0025 and the torture bonus; no vote for the accused after a confession (success) or a guilty plea
2026-11-05T09:30:54 0x004946c0 data ai_Unk4946c0 -> ai_DecideSentence by:main why:the trial's ask-AI callback ai_Unk4de340 answers request kind 5 with it (the judge m[7] = ids[2], checked as cm_TrialAskPlayer's case 5): cm_RunTrial takes the answer as the sentence (sentence = the answer, gv_CheckSentence(c1, i + rank), the texts rank * 3 + 0x1534 + i * 3), so the returned number is the sentence index of the plan's rank raised by the judge's liking of the accused (ai_PlanRank, gm_Liking against k * 66.666 / 33.333 where k = 0.7 + (5 - record 0's cur) * 0.1), with 5 -> 4 for a judge without office and 7 -> 6 for a judge under rank 2
2026-11-05T09:32:05 0x004948f0 func ai_Unk4948f0 -> ai_RollStudyOffers by:main why:fills three study offers (a price, two subject indexes) for a character: ai_DecideStudy (action 0x3b, decide callback) takes one of them (G8_4948F0, o1 kind 7 / o2 kind 0xe, the price rec.a * 10, the subjects rec.b / rec.c as JOBTALENTS.skills) and the 'special_uni' identity window (ai_Unk5cf4f0, 0x5cf4f0) lists a row per player slot with the player name and the offer's two subject texts; the price is the character's worth * 0.025 split by the map distance from player slot 0's place (ai_PlayerSlots + 0x40 / +0x44) to slots 1 .. 3's places
2026-11-05T09:33:15 0x00494a30 data ai_Unk494a30 -> ai_MasterExamPassed by:main why:the guild master's exam decision of the master exam event he_Unk543ac0 (he.c 0x543ac0, 'Berufe\Messagebox_Meisterpruefung'): it calls it with the guild master (cr) and the examinee (me) and reads 0 as passed back (h = (h == 1) ? 0 : 1; h 0 = passed 0x1785, 1 = failed 0x1786), so 1 is a pass. The body: 0 when the master's partner is the examinee (netId == partner), else 1 when the liking of the examinee plus 2.5 per level the examinee is above the master reaches a random * 75
